"""Curated seed knowledge base (KB v1.0.0).

Every interaction row carries: severity, interaction_type, mechanism, effect, management, optional timing gap,
evidence grade (A/B/C), population flags, sources, and review metadata.

SOURCE POLICY: nothing here is marked `verified`. Each source is listed with the identifiers the team believes are
correct and `verification_status = needs_verification`. A team member must open every DOI/URL, confirm it, and set
the status to `verified` (scripts/verify_sources.py prints the checklist). Nothing is presented to users as verified
until that is done. No citation has been invented to fill a gap: where a claim rests on tertiary sources only
(monograph / database), that is what is cited and the evidence grade reflects it.

Drug classes used: thyroid_hormone, anticoagulant, antiplatelet, antidiabetic, antihypertensive, diuretic,
cardiac_glycoside, immunosuppressant, corticosteroid, statin, ssri, benzodiazepine, antiepileptic, mood_stabiliser,
iron, antibiotic.  '*' = applies to any drug (route-aware for timing rows).
"""
from __future__ import annotations

REVIEWER = "TakeSure curation team (pending external pharmacologist review)"
REVIEWED_ON = "2026-09-20"
KB_VERSION = "1.0.0"

